WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.872
Several trolls were waiting when Morb arrived back at the fortress.

2
00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.914
The leader, an especially large and ugly troll, grunted.

3
00:00:10.915 --> 00:00:17.292
A fuzzy image of a figure trapped behind iron bars appeared briefly above his head before quickly fading out.

4
00:00:17.293 --> 00:00:25.261
Morb tried to hide his disdain. Trolls were disgusting creatures, with their rough magic and rougher appetites.

5
00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:28.083
But he needed them, at least for now.

6
00:00:28.084 --> 00:00:31.283
"Prepare the treatment!" he ordered the troll.

7
00:00:31.284 --> 00:00:40.057
The troll lumbered off. Morb strode across the room and down a steep stone stairwell.

8
00:00:40.058 --> 00:00:42.613
At the bottom was a heavy wooden door.

9
00:00:42.614 --> 00:00:46.587
As soon as he pushed it open, the prisoners began crying out.

10
00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:52.577
There were now more than a dozen of them in the cells, peering out from behind the heavy iron bars.

11
00:00:52.578 --> 00:00:54.988
But Morb barely looked at most of them.

12
00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:58.318
His eyes went directly to one particular cell.

13
00:00:58.319 --> 00:01:02.318
The long-nosed old man inside stared back defiantly.

14
00:01:02.319 --> 00:01:06.288
His hands and legs were tied so he couldn't move without falling over. But

15
00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:09.551
he stood tall and proud despite the restraints. "You!"

16
00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:13.425
Boz spat out as Morb approached. "I

17
00:01:13.426 --> 00:01:16.703
should have guessed when I heard the news. You

18
00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:20.031
never could accept that you weren't meant to—" "Silence!"

19
00:01:20.032 --> 00:01:27.012
Morb cut him off. He turned toward the door. "I'm ready!" he called loudly. Heavy

20
00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:34.312
footsteps tromped down the stairs. A pair of trolls came in, lugging an iron cauldron between them. The

21
00:01:34.313 --> 00:01:37.156
prisoners shrank back fearfully when they saw it. All

22
00:01:37.157 --> 00:01:42.051
except Boz. "What are you going to do, Morb?" he demanded. "Feed

23
00:01:42.052 --> 00:01:48.158
me to your pet trolls? The Red Council will hear about this, have no doubt. Using

24
00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:55.561
Flash Freezes and Dousing spells, holding people prisoner . . . You won't get away with it!" Morb

25
00:01:55.562 --> 00:02:00.045
ignored him. The trolls tipped the cauldron, spilling its contents. Leeches.

26
00:02:00.046 --> 00:02:04.314
Dozens of enormous pale blue leeches. Their

27
00:02:04.315 --> 00:02:06.613
faces turned this way and that. They

28
00:02:06.614 --> 00:02:10.904
could sense the powerful magic of all the Red prisoners nearby. "Get

29
00:02:10.905 --> 00:02:18.241
Boz," Morb said. The leeches slowly wriggled between the bars and into Boz's cell. Boz

30
00:02:18.242 --> 00:02:23.361
looked startled. "Where did those things come from?" he exclaimed. "There

31
00:02:23.362 --> 00:02:28.901
are no leeches that size anywhere in Magica! How did you— ahh

32
00:02:28.902 --> 00:02:32.936
!" The rest of his words were lost as the leeches slithered up his

33
00:02:32.937 --> 00:02:38.515
legs. Their pale bodies brightened to a vivid electric blue as they fed on Boz's

34
00:02:38.516 --> 00:02:43.661
magic. Morb watched for a moment, enjoying the sight. Then he turned

35
00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:49.160
away. He still had unfinished business to deal with before he could put the rest of his plan into

36
00:02:49.161 --> 00:02:56.310
motion. He hurried back upstairs, pulled out the picture he'd taken from Boz's house, and carefully ripped out the boy's

37
00:02:56.311 --> 00:03:02.084
face. Morb then stepped toward the Secret Eye, his gaze on the ancient skull at the

38
00:03:02.085 --> 00:03:04.336
top. Then he noticed a flutter of

39
00:03:04.337 --> 00:03:09.148
movement. Turning his head, he saw an insect hovering just outside the window.

40
00:03:09.149 --> 00:03:15.768
"A spy fly!" he murmured. "Now who would want to spy on little old me?"

41
00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:20.025
The spy fly sensed it had been spotted. It spun around to fly off.

42
00:03:20.026 --> 00:03:22.353
But Morb was too quick for it.

43
00:03:22.354 --> 00:03:29.481
Rubbing his fingers together, he blew it to pieces with an extra-strong Flash Freeze.

44
00:03:29.482 --> 00:03:34.530
Then he gently placed the Red boy's picture into one of the skull's eye sockets.

45
00:03:34.531 --> 00:03:40.600
Stepping back, he watched as the map above slowly started to change.

46
00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:44.707
"Stay here," Zann ordered Zing. "We'll be back soon."

47
00:03:44.708 --> 00:03:50.237
The dragon spat fire at him. Zann rolled his eyes.

48
00:03:50.238 --> 00:03:53.983
"Let me talk to him." Darb knelt in front of Zing.

49
00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:58.267
"Listen, buddy. We need you to guard the cave while we check on Gliss, okay?"

50
00:03:58.268 --> 00:04:01.427
Zing continued to look skeptical for a second.

51
00:04:01.428 --> 00:04:05.627
Then finally he whistled happily, wriggling his whole body.

52
00:04:05.628 --> 00:04:11.686
Zann sighed. The dragon never could resist Darb's charms. It was kind of annoying.

53
00:04:11.687 --> 00:04:16.914
"Let's go," Perda said, grabbing Darb's hand. "I've got Darb."

54
00:04:16.915 --> 00:04:21.898
"Meet you in Gliss' living room." Zann closed his eyes, focusing his mind.

55
00:04:21.899 --> 00:04:24.684
This was no time to be sloppy.

56
00:04:24.685 --> 00:04:27.124
He'd been in Gliss' house several times.

57
00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:31.651
Her parents were always inviting him over. It was actually a little embarrassing.

58
00:04:31.652 --> 00:04:39.488
They seemed to think that because Zann and Gliss were the only two Reds in their level, they should be friends. Maybe even more than friends.

59
00:04:39.489 --> 00:04:42.179
Zann tried not to get distracted by that.

60
00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.027
He and Gliss weren't especially close, but he liked her fine.

61
00:04:46.028 --> 00:04:50.897
He definitely didn't want to see her captured by this Morb character.

62
00:04:50.898 --> 00:04:54.977
"Zap," he whispered.

63
00:04:54.978 --> 00:04:59.748
Bam ! He landed hard on the ground with the wind knocked out of

64
00:04:59.749 --> 00:05:03.388
him. Opening his eyes, he saw Gliss'

65
00:05:03.389 --> 00:05:10.140
house. "Oof!" Perda grunted beside him. She and Darb appeared, both of them also flung off their

66
00:05:10.141 --> 00:05:12.564
feet. "What happened?" Darb

67
00:05:12.565 --> 00:05:16.679
asked. Zann stood up, wincing. "They must have a Shield spell up."

68
00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:21.250
"No wonder," Perda said. "They're probably worried about the warning.

69
00:05:21.251 --> 00:05:24.003
But it means we're blocked out too."

70
00:05:24.004 --> 00:05:34.319
"No big deal," Darb said. "It is possible to get into a house without using magic, you know." He smiled. "It's called knocking on the door."

71
00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.098
"Zann!" Gliss' mother exclaimed when she answered the door.

72
00:05:38.099 --> 00:05:41.834
"You shouldn't be out right now. Haven't you heard the news?"

73
00:05:41.835 --> 00:05:44.383
She quickly ushered all the kids inside.

74
00:05:44.384 --> 00:05:47.108
Her husband and Gliss were in the main room.

75
00:05:47.109 --> 00:05:51.300
"You're okay!" Perda exclaimed, rushing over to Gliss.

76
00:05:51.301 --> 00:05:56.855
"Listen," Zann told Gliss' parents. "We just figured out who's behind all the trouble."

77
00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.182
"You did?" Gliss' father said.

78
00:05:59.183 --> 00:06:03.277
"I'll show you." Zann snapped his fingers to call up the Directory.

79
00:06:03.278 --> 00:06:06.236
"Morb," he said when the book appeared.

80
00:06:06.237 --> 00:06:10.732
But before the image could fully form, there was a sudden, blinding flash.

81
00:06:10.733 --> 00:06:15.451
The next thing Zann knew, a familiar figure was standing before him.

82
00:06:15.452 --> 00:06:24.806
"You called?" Morb said with a sneer.

